{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Review-plan run 2 PASS (0 blocking). Its advisories showed store_freshness and claim_gate_check also serve read-only, network-free queries (review-plan --status, MCP plan_review_status, plan-review reuse), so a heal inside them would add a fetch and a store mutation to a read-only query. Plan revised: the heal (freshness.heal_if_superseded, lock-free only) runs at the 4 mutating gate entries instead; the probes stay pure. AC unchanged; re-running review-plan."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795253758885103001,"uuid":"6b246aab-c2b1-4dcd-b7ff-c508c1ad553d"}